1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,605
Before you walk out that door
today, give me a few minutes.

2
00:00:04,163 --> 00:00:06,105
You already know what's out there.

3
00:00:06,663 --> 00:00:08,625
The email you've been dreading.

4
00:00:09,183 --> 00:00:10,250
The drive.

5
00:00:10,808 --> 00:00:13,112
The conversation you keep putting off.

6
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:16,894
And you're about to walk
into all of it with nothing

7
00:00:16,894 --> 00:00:19,622
between you and the day
but a cup of coffee.

8
00:00:21,305 --> 00:00:24,441
This psalm is for the person
standing at that door.

9
00:00:24,999 --> 00:00:28,199
People have prayed it in
hospital hallways, before

10
00:00:28,199 --> 00:00:31,783
shifts, and on the way to
jobs they were scared to lose.

11
00:00:32,341 --> 00:00:34,261
Pray it with me, and then go.

12
00:00:36,644 --> 00:00:38,393
Here is how it starts.

13
00:00:38,951 --> 00:00:41,661
Psalm 91, verses 1 and 2.

14
00:00:43,794 --> 00:00:48,072
He that dwelleth in the secret
place of the most High shall

15
00:00:48,072 --> 00:00:52,640
abide under the shadow of the
Almighty. I will say of the LORD,

16
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:57,063
He is my refuge and my fortress:
my God; in him will I trust.

17
00:00:59,223 --> 00:01:00,823
Look at the word dwelleth.

18
00:01:01,381 --> 00:01:03,280
That's somebody who lives there.

19
00:01:03,838 --> 00:01:07,358
Not a person who stops by
when the car breaks down.

20
00:01:07,916 --> 00:01:10,866
This one is for an ordinary Tuesday, when

21
00:01:10,866 --> 00:01:13,889
nobody is watching and nothing is on fire.

22
00:01:14,447 --> 00:01:17,215
When's the last time you
prayed before you left

23
00:01:17,215 --> 00:01:20,100
the house, instead of
after something went wrong?

24
00:01:21,783 --> 00:01:24,514
And look at what the
writer does in verse 2.

25
00:01:25,072 --> 00:01:26,672
He says it out loud.

26
00:01:27,230 --> 00:01:28,958
I will say of the LORD.

27
00:01:29,516 --> 00:01:31,863
Your worry talks all morning long.

28
00:01:32,421 --> 00:01:34,106
Faith has to talk back.

29
00:01:36,489 --> 00:01:38,110
Verses 3 and 4.

30
00:01:40,243 --> 00:01:44,831
Surely he shall deliver thee from
the snare of the fowler, and from the

31
00:01:44,831 --> 00:01:49,224
noisome pestilence. He shall cover
thee with his feathers, and under

32
00:01:49,224 --> 00:01:53,747
his wings shalt thou trust: his truth
shall be thy shield and buckler.

33
00:01:55,907 --> 00:02:00,643
A fowler is a trapper, and a snare
is the trap you never saw coming.

34
00:02:01,201 --> 00:02:02,417
The bad deal.

35
00:02:02,975 --> 00:02:04,277
The wrong crowd.

36
00:02:04,835 --> 00:02:06,733
The text you should not have sent.

37
00:02:07,291 --> 00:02:10,470
God sees the trap before
you ever step toward it.

38
00:02:12,153 --> 00:02:14,180
Then comes the picture I love.

39
00:02:14,738 --> 00:02:16,103
Under his wings.

40
00:02:16,661 --> 00:02:20,620
A mother bird covers her young
with her own body when the weather

41
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:24,213
turns, and whatever is coming
has to get through her first.

42
00:02:26,596 --> 00:02:28,281
Verses 5 through 8.

43
00:02:30,414 --> 00:02:35,314
Thou shalt not be afraid for the
terror by night; nor for the arrow that

44
00:02:35,314 --> 00:02:40,146
flieth by day; Nor for the pestilence
that walketh in darkness; nor for

45
00:02:40,146 --> 00:02:45,250
the destruction that wasteth at noonday.
A thousand shall fall at thy side,

46
00:02:45,250 --> 00:02:49,877
and ten thousand at thy right hand;
but it shall not come nigh thee.

47
00:02:49,877 --> 00:02:54,777
Only with thine eyes shalt thou behold
and see the reward of the wicked.

48
00:02:56,937 --> 00:03:01,737
Four hours are named in there, the
night, the day, the darkness, and noon.

49
00:03:02,295 --> 00:03:05,666
There is no hour on the clock
that was left uncovered.

50
00:03:06,224 --> 00:03:10,055
The fear that hits at three in
the morning is on that list,

51
00:03:10,055 --> 00:03:13,562
and so is the trouble that
shows up in broad daylight.

52
00:03:15,245 --> 00:03:18,957
So does that mean nothing bad
ever comes near a believer?

53
00:03:19,515 --> 00:03:20,881
Read it again.

54
00:03:21,439 --> 00:03:23,956
It never says nothing will come at you.

55
00:03:24,514 --> 00:03:27,181
It says you do not have
to be afraid of it.

56
00:03:27,739 --> 00:03:33,328
Jesus said the same thing plainly,
in John chapter 16, verse 33.

57
00:03:35,461 --> 00:03:40,944
These things I have spoken unto you, that
in me ye might have peace. In the world

58
00:03:40,944 --> 00:03:46,021
ye shall have tribulation: but be of
good cheer; I have overcome the world.

59
00:03:48,881 --> 00:03:50,268
Back to the psalm.

60
00:03:50,826 --> 00:03:52,404
Verses 9 and 10.

61
00:03:54,537 --> 00:03:58,526
Because thou hast made the
LORD, which is my refuge, even

62
00:03:58,526 --> 00:04:02,514
the most High, thy habitation;
There shall no evil befall

63
00:04:02,514 --> 00:04:06,292
thee, neither shall any
plague come nigh thy dwelling.

64
00:04:08,452 --> 00:04:09,903
Thy habitation.

65
00:04:10,461 --> 00:04:12,786
It keeps coming back to where you live.

66
00:04:13,344 --> 00:04:17,077
Proverbs chapter 18, verse
10 puts it another way.

67
00:04:19,210 --> 00:04:22,041
The name of the LORD
is a strong tower: the

68
00:04:22,041 --> 00:04:24,608
righteous runneth into it, and is safe.

69
00:04:26,768 --> 00:04:28,069
Runneth into it.

70
00:04:28,627 --> 00:04:30,568
So when the fear comes, run.

71
00:04:31,126 --> 00:04:32,321
Say his name.

72
00:04:32,879 --> 00:04:34,628
You don't need fancy words.

73
00:04:35,186 --> 00:04:37,704
Jesus, help me, is a whole prayer.

74
00:04:40,087 --> 00:04:42,049
Verses 11 through 13.

75
00:04:44,182 --> 00:04:48,620
For he shall give his angels charge
over thee, to keep thee in all

76
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:52,923
thy ways. They shall bear thee
up in their hands, lest thou dash

77
00:04:52,923 --> 00:04:56,957
thy foot against a stone. Thou
shalt tread upon the lion and

78
00:04:56,957 --> 00:05:01,462
adder: the young lion and the dragon
shalt thou trample under feet.

79
00:05:03,622 --> 00:05:05,244
You have help you can't see.

80
00:05:05,802 --> 00:05:08,532
God gives his angels orders about you.

81
00:05:09,090 --> 00:05:12,653
How many close calls have
you already walked away from?

82
00:05:13,211 --> 00:05:17,094
You have probably been kept from
things you will never hear about.

83
00:05:17,652 --> 00:05:19,806
The truck that did not cross the line.

84
00:05:20,364 --> 00:05:23,948
The night you made it home when
you had no business making it.

85
00:05:25,631 --> 00:05:27,125
One careful note.

86
00:05:27,683 --> 00:05:30,903
The devil set Jesus on
the top of the temple,

87
00:05:30,903 --> 00:05:34,339
quoted these very verses,
and dared him to jump.

88
00:05:34,897 --> 00:05:36,326
Jesus said no.

89
00:05:36,884 --> 00:05:40,404
This psalm is a shelter for
people who walk with God.

90
00:05:40,962 --> 00:05:44,503
It was never a permission
slip to go looking for danger.

91
00:05:46,886 --> 00:05:50,577
Now listen, because in
verse 14 the voice changes.

92
00:05:51,135 --> 00:05:53,332
God himself starts to talk.

93
00:05:53,890 --> 00:05:55,981
Verses 14 through 16.

94
00:05:58,114 --> 00:06:02,914
Because he hath set his love upon me,
therefore will I deliver him: I will

95
00:06:02,914 --> 00:06:07,715
set him on high, because he hath known
my name. He shall call upon me, and

96
00:06:07,715 --> 00:06:12,450
I will answer him: I will be with him
in trouble; I will deliver him, and

97
00:06:12,450 --> 00:06:17,186
honour him. With long life will I
satisfy him, and shew him my salvation.

98
00:06:19,346 --> 00:06:20,903
Look at the middle of that.

99
00:06:21,461 --> 00:06:23,467
I will be with him in trouble.

100
00:06:24,025 --> 00:06:27,118
He never said you would
not see trouble today.

101
00:06:27,676 --> 00:06:29,959
He said you would not be in it alone.

102
00:06:31,642 --> 00:06:33,071
And look at the reason.

103
00:06:33,629 --> 00:06:35,720
Because he hath set his love upon me.

104
00:06:36,278 --> 00:06:40,246
This whole psalm rests on a
relationship, not a formula.

105
00:06:40,804 --> 00:06:45,049
If you have drifted, this morning
is a good morning to walk back.

106
00:06:47,432 --> 00:06:49,075
So here is the prayer.

107
00:06:49,633 --> 00:06:51,766
Pray it out loud if you can.

108
00:06:53,449 --> 00:06:58,420
Father, I am stepping out the door, and
I am putting this day under your wing.

109
00:06:58,978 --> 00:07:01,154
Cover my house while I am gone.

110
00:07:01,712 --> 00:07:05,018
Cover the ones I love,
wherever they are right now.

111
00:07:05,576 --> 00:07:08,606
When a trap is set, show me before I step.

112
00:07:09,164 --> 00:07:12,129
When fear comes, remind me where I dwell.

113
00:07:12,687 --> 00:07:15,172
Send your angels ahead of me, and let me

114
00:07:15,172 --> 00:07:17,658
come home tonight with a thankful heart.

115
00:07:18,216 --> 00:07:20,904
I ask it in the name of Jesus Christ.

116
00:07:21,462 --> 00:07:22,528
Amen.

117
00:07:24,211 --> 00:07:27,518
Type amen, and send this
to a friend who needs it.

118
00:07:28,076 --> 00:07:31,447
Have a blessed day, and
remember the Word for today.

